# Workflow: LEARNING-GATE

Purpose:
  Define the learning gate — the checkpoint at end of task execution
  where the AI asks: "Did we learn anything?" This is the execution
  layer of the "AI improves itself as it works" principle. Knowledge
  is classified and either discarded, archived, linked, or promoted
  into persistent knowledge.

Owns:
  Learning gate classification
  Knowledge promotion paths
  Negative knowledge registration

LearningGate:

  definition: checkpoint before task completion where knowledge
              extracted during execution is evaluated
  position: after DOCUMENTATION, before CONSOLIDATION (bax
            execution-loop.sdd)

  Question: Did we learn anything?

  Outcomes:

    NO_NEW_KNOWLEDGE
      meaning: no new learning occurred; all knowledge was already
               covered by existing references and skills
      action: discard runtime observations, archive trace
      requirement: must justify why no new knowledge (e.g., routine
                   task, no novel approach needed)

    EXISTING_KNOWLEDGE_UPDATED
      meaning: an existing skill, decision, or reference was
               confirmed, refined, or its context expanded
      action: link execution evidence to existing knowledge artifact
      example: @skill.payment.idempotency confirmed valid in
               new context (refund flow)

    NEW_CANDIDATE
      meaning: a new pattern or approach was observed that may be
               valuable but is not yet validated
      action: register as candidate with evidence trace
      artifact: @candidate.<name>
      rule: candidates expire (default 30 days) unless validated

    NEW_VALIDATED_SKILL
      meaning: a genuinely new, validated, reusable skill was
               discovered and demonstrated
      action: promote to @skill.* with full metadata
      artifact: @skill.<name>
      requirement: must have evidence (code, test, task link)

    NEW_DECISION
      meaning: a new project-level decision was made during
               execution (architecture, approach, trade-off)
      action: create decision record (bax decisions/)
      artifact: @decision.<name>
      requirement: decision MUST be recorded before COMPLETED

    NEW_LESSON
      meaning: a failed approach or rejected pattern was learned
      action: register in negative knowledge / rejected approaches
      artifact: @rejected.<name>
      requirement: includes reason + preferred alternative

KnowledgePromotion:

  flow:
    Runtime Observation -> Classification -> Action

  paths:
    observation is routine
      -> NO_NEW_KNOWLEDGE (discard)

    observation confirms existing knowledge
      -> EXISTING_KNOWLEDGE_UPDATED (link evidence)

    observation is novel but unvalidated
      -> NEW_CANDIDATE (register with TTL)

    observation is novel, validated, and reusable
      -> NEW_VALIDATED_SKILL (promote to @skill.*)

    execution produced a decision
      -> NEW_DECISION (create @decision.*)

    execution tried an approach that failed
      -> NEW_LESSON (register @rejected.*)

  rules:
    [KG1] Every NEW_VALIDATED_SKILL MUST have code or test evidence.
    [KG2] Every NEW_DECISION MUST be recorded before COMPLETED.
    [KG3] NEW_CANDIDATE without validation within TTL is archived.
    [KG4] Negative knowledge (@rejected.*) is retained permanently
          as @lessons (bax lessons/).
    [KG5] Knowledge promoted to ESTABLISHED status requires human
          verification (bax concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd).

KnowledgeArtifacts:

  candidate:
    prefix: @candidate.
    schema:
      name: <identifier>
      discovered: <task_id>
      evidence: [<trace_refs>]
      status: candidate
      ttl: 30d

  skill:
    prefix: @skill.
    schema:
      name: <identifier>
      discovered: <task_id>
      evidence: [<code_refs, test_refs>]
      status: validated
      related_skills: [<skill_refs>]

  decision:
    prefix: @decision.
    schema:
      name: <identifier>
      discovered: <task_id>
      evidence: [<trace_refs>]
      status: implemented
      related_decisions: [<decision_refs>]

  lesson:
    prefix: @rejected.
    schema:
      name: <identifier>
      discovered: <task_id>
      failed_approach: <description>
      preferred: <alternative>
      reason: <why it failed>

Consolidation:

  definition: collapse runtime trace (100+ events) into persistent artifacts
  flow:
    1. Review execution trace
    2. Identify decisions, skills, lessons
    3. Drop temporary observations
    4. Archive ambiguous items
    5. Link confirmed items to existing knowledge
    6. Promote new validated items

  example:
    100 execution events
      -> 3 important decisions (@decision.*)
      -> 1 new skill (@skill.*)
      -> 2 rejected approaches (@rejected.*)

Rules:

  [LG1] The learning gate MUST run before task COMPLETED.
  [LG2] NO_NEW_KNOWLEDGE MUST be explicitly justified.
  [LG3] NEW_DECISION artifacts MUST be recorded before completion.
  [LG4] NEW_VALIDATED_SKILLs MUST include evidence links.
  [LG5] Negative knowledge MUST be retained — never silently deleted.
  [LG6] Candidates without validation within TTL are archived, not
        deleted.
  [LG7] Knowledge promotion follows the trust hierarchy (see
        LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd -> TrustHierarchy).
  [LG8] All learning gate outcomes MUST be recorded in execution summary.
  [LG9] New skills that duplicate existing canonical concepts MUST
        link to the canonical concept instead of creating duplicates.
  [LG10] Learning gate is the feedback loop that drives system evolution.

Navigation:

  ExecutionLoop: @execution-loop.sdd
  PartialDone: @../tasks/PARTIAL-DONE.sdd
  KnowledgeModel: @../concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd
  HumanDocsGate: @human-docs-gate.sdd
  RejectedApproaches: @../lessons/INDEX.sdd
  TasksIndex: @../tasks/INDEX.sdd

State: +
